.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH acc-verify 1  "verify 0.7.0" 
.SH NAME
acc\-verify \- Gate a deploy: every first\-parent commit in a range must be landed by a change that a signed acc attestation shows passing
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBacc verify\fR [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-verification\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-signer\fR] [\fB\-\-issuer\fR] [\fB\-\-attestations\fR] [\fB\-\-verified\-by\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\fR] [\fB\-\-as\-of\fR] [\fB\-\-checkout\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fB\-\-range\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Gate a deploy: every first\-parent commit in a range must be landed by a change that a signed acc attestation shows passing
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress status lines on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-range\fR \fI<BASE..HEAD>\fR
The commits to cover, as BASE..HEAD: the commit deployed last and the one about to be. Every first\-parent commit after BASE up to and including HEAD must be covered
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print extra diagnostics on stderr (resolved policy, format, destination, counts). Never changes stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-verification\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
A verifier\*(Aqs JSON output (`gh attestation verify \-\-format json`), whose bundles hold acc attestations (repeatable; requires \-\-signer)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Never color diagnostics. acc\*(Aqs own output is never colored; this and a non\-empty NO_COLOR environment variable switch off color in help and usage errors too
.TP
\fB\-\-signer\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
A certificate identity the gate trusts to sign verdicts, compared exactly with the verifier\*(Aqs subject alternative name, for example https://github.com/acme/api/.github/workflows/attest.yml@refs/heads/main (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-issuer\fR \fI<URL>\fR
The OIDC issuer the signer\*(Aqs identity must come from, for example https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com
.TP
\fB\-\-attestations\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Signed DSSE envelopes or Sigstore bundles (.json or .jsonl, files or directories) whose signatures the caller has verified (repeatable; requires \-\-verified\-by)
.TP
\fB\-\-verified\-by\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Who verified the \-\-attestations signatures, and against which identity, recorded verbatim in the result
.TP
\fB\-\-policy\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Policy file; overrides the policy embedded in each attestation
.TP
\fB\-\-as\-of\fR \fI<DATE>\fR
Calendar date dispositions are evaluated on (YYYY\-MM\-DD). Required when a signed finding has a non\-open disposition; the machine clock is never consulted
.TP
\fB\-\-checkout\fR \fI<DIR>\fR [default: .]
The local clone the range is read from
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Result format: `text` (one line per commit) or `json` (a result object); inferred from the \-\-output extension when omitted
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text: One status line; `table` is an alias
.IP \(bu 2
json: One JSON object (RFC 8785 bytes) followed by a newline
.RE
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the result to FILE instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.7.0
